# Files the CI consumes byte-exactly keep LF endings on every
# checkout. On the Windows runner, git's default core.autocrlf=true
# otherwise rewrites text files to CRLF in the worktree:
#   * git apply matches patch context byte-for-byte, so a CRLF
#     patch file can never apply to the LF tree. Build #14 failed
#     exactly this way at scripts/ci/lumo_patches/0001 (forward and
#     reverse checks both failed at the first hunk), while
#     Thorium's own patches were immune because Thorium's
#     .gitattributes pins this same rule. Pin it here too.
#   * The branding images are copied into the browser tree
#     verbatim by stage.py; keep git from ever treating them as
#     text.
*.patch text eol=lf
scripts/ci/lumo_branding/*.ico binary
scripts/ci/lumo_branding/*.png binary
